From fe6b91e708a45fb1b628d089ad8e2cfba579ad70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:43:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] buildroot: SLIP default 2000000 on the arm64 family,
 fallback 1000000
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the uart reclock the arm64 boards generate the modem's factory
2 Mbaud exactly, so the shipped slip.conf/S31slip defaults stop
papering over the old 25 MHz/16 = 1,562,500 ceiling with 1500000 (which
only fit the line to +4.17% anyway). Fallback advice becomes 1000000 —
also exact at 96 MHz (quot 6) — replacing 921600, which is -7% there.

This is a DELTA OVERRIDE of the shared licheerv-nano 0022, not an amend
of it: the shared series stays byte-identical across the rnsbox repos
and keeps the Nano-correct 1500000 default for boards without the 96 MHz
reclock; the delta that introduces the capability carries the default
flip, and only the arm64 family consumes this series.
---
 README.RNSBox.md                              | 56 +++++++++++--------
 .../cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip  |  2 +-
 .../SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf       | 18 +++---
 3 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.RNSBox.md b/README.RNSBox.md
index cae084412..6ac8c2026 100644
--- a/README.RNSBox.md
+++ b/README.RNSBox.md
@@ -111,43 +111,51 @@ as a long-range sub-GHz Reticulum interface, connected over a 3-wire UART using
 ### Wiring — pinout
 
 Use **UART1** = `/dev/ttyS1` — **not** `ttyS0`, which is the Linux serial
-console. On the LicheeRV Nano-e, UART1 is the two pads labelled **`GPIOA28`**
-(SoC function `UART1_TX`) and **`GPIOA29`** (`UART1_RX`) on Sipeed's pinout
-diagram; take **GND** from any ground pad on the same header. All three lines are
-**3.3 V TTL** — never wire a 5 V or RS-232 level.
+console. On the rnsbox CVITEK boards, UART1 is the two pads **`XGPIOA[28]`**
+(SoC function `UART1_TX`) and **`XGPIOA[29]`** (`UART1_RX`) — labelled
+`GPIOA28`/`GPIOA29` on Sipeed's pinout diagrams; u-boot muxes the pads at
+boot (cvi_board_init.c). On a Milk-V Duo carrier check the header silk for
+the A28/A29 route. Take **GND** from any ground pad on the same header. All
+three lines are **3.3 V TTL** — never wire a 5 V or RS-232 level.
 
 TX and RX must **cross over** — the box's TX goes to the modem's RX and vice
 versa:
 
 ```
-  LicheeRV Nano-e (UART1 / ttyS1)                  HaLow RNode modem
+  RNSBox CVITEK (UART1 / ttyS1)                    HaLow RNode modem
   ─────────────────────────────────                ─────────────────
-   GPIOA28  ·  UART1_TX  ─────────────────────────►  RX
-   GPIOA29  ·  UART1_RX  ◄─────────────────────────  TX
+   XGPIOA[28] ·  UART1_TX  ────────────────────────►  RX
+   XGPIOA[29] ·  UART1_RX  ◄────────────────────────  TX
    GND                   ────────────────────────── GND   (required)
 ```
 
-| Nano-e pad | Function | Wire to modem |
-|------------|----------|---------------|
-| `GPIOA28`  | UART1_TX | RX            |
-| `GPIOA29`  | UART1_RX | TX            |
-| `GND`      | ground   | GND           |
+| Board pad   | Function | Wire to modem |
+|-------------|----------|---------------|
+| `XGPIOA[28]` | UART1_TX | RX            |
+| `XGPIOA[29]` | UART1_RX | TX            |
+| `GND`        | ground   | GND           |
 
-Keep the leads short — at 1.5 Mbaud, long unshielded jumpers invite frame errors.
+Keep the leads short — at 2 Mbaud, long unshielded jumpers invite frame errors.
 
 ### Baud
 
-Both ends must run the **same baud**. The Nano-e's UART is clocked from 25 MHz,
-so its ceiling is **1,562,500** (25 MHz / 16) — it cannot reach the modem's
-2,000,000 default. Use **1500000** on both sides:
-
-- **Modem**: set SLIP baud to `1500000` over its Ethernet web UI (or `POST
-  /api/slip_cfg`). Runtime-settable and persisted — no reflash.
-- **RNSBox**: `baud=1500000` in the *HaLow modem (SLIP)* card (or
-  `/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf`).
-
-If `rx_over_errors` climbs under load (`ip -s link show sl0`), drop both ends to
-`1000000` or `921600`.
+Both ends must run the **same baud**. On the rnsbox CVITEK arm64 boards
+(SG2000 / SG2002 on the Cortex-A53) the kernel reclocks `clk_cam0_200` to
+96 MHz (disppll/8) before the 8250 probes, so the modem's factory
+**2000000** is generated **exactly** (96 MHz / 16 / 3) — keep it on both
+sides:
+
+- **Modem**: leave the factory SLIP baud `2000000` (verify in its Ethernet
+  web UI, or `POST /api/slip_cfg`). Runtime-settable and persisted — no
+  reflash.
+- **RNSBox**: `baud=2000000` in the *HaLow modem (SLIP)* card (or
+  `/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf` — the shipped default on these boards).
+
+If `rx_over_errors` climbs under load (`ip -s link show sl0`), drop **both
+ends** to `1000000` (also exact on these boards: 96 MHz / 16 / 6). On
+boards without the 96 MHz reclock — e.g. the LicheeRV Nano-e, whose UART
+runs from 25 MHz and tops out at **1,562,500** — use `1500000` on both
+sides instead.
 
 ### Bring it up
 
diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
index 6f220d562..8e292b836 100755
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ start() {
 	case "$enabled" in yes|true|1|on) ;; *) echo "S31slip: disabled"; return 0 ;; esac
 
 	device=$(cfg device);     [ -n "$device" ]   || device=/dev/ttyS1
-	baud=$(cfg baud);         [ -n "$baud" ]     || baud=1500000
+	baud=$(cfg baud);         [ -n "$baud" ]     || baud=2000000
 	local_ip=$(cfg local_ip); [ -n "$local_ip" ] || local_ip=192.168.7.1
 	peer_ip=$(cfg peer_ip);   [ -n "$peer_ip" ]  || peer_ip=192.168.7.2
 
diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
index 207320d47..1c31050cd 100644
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
@@ -10,17 +10,21 @@
 #       target_host = 192.168.7.2      # = peer_ip below
 #       target_port = 4242
 #
-# Wiring (LicheeRV Nano-e): UART1 on GPIOA28 (TX) / GPIOA29 (RX), 3.3 V,
-# common ground — device = /dev/ttyS1. Do NOT use ttyS0 (console).
+# Wiring (rnsbox CVITEK arm64 boards): UART1 on XGPIOA[28] (TX) /
+# XGPIOA[29] (RX), 3.3 V, common ground — device = /dev/ttyS1. Do NOT use
+# ttyS0 (console).
 #
-# baud MUST match the modem's SLIP baud. The Nano's UART tops out at
-# 1,562,500 (25 MHz/16); the modem defaults to 2,000,000 which the Nano
-# cannot reach, so set the modem to 1500000 (via its web UI) and match it
-# here. local_ip/peer_ip must match the modem's SLIP config (defaults
+# baud MUST match the modem's SLIP baud. On the boards in this series the
+# kernel reclocks clk_cam0_200 to disppll/8 = 96 MHz before the 8250
+# probes, so the modem's factory 2000000 is generated exactly
+# (96M/16/3) — keep it. Fallback with headroom for frame errors:
+# 1000000 (also exact, 96M/16/6). At the old fixed 25 MHz uart clock the
+# 8250 ceiling was 1,562,500, which is what 1500000 was papering over.
+# local_ip/peer_ip must match the modem's SLIP config (defaults
 # 192.168.7.2 device / 192.168.7.1 host).
 
 enabled=no
 device=/dev/ttyS1
-baud=1500000
+baud=2000000
 local_ip=192.168.7.1
 peer_ip=192.168.7.2
